            <article class="about-content">
                <p class="about-label">Bachelor thesis project</p>
                <h1>Malaria DeepLearning</h1>
                <p>
                    This web application was developed as part of the thesis
                    <strong>Development of web application and convolutional neural network for the image classification of human cells infected by malaria.</strong>
                    The project combines a browser-based interface with a trained Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) for classifying red blood cell images.
                </p>
                <p>
                    The frontend allows users to upload one or more cell images and adjust the classification threshold before analysis. The backend loads the trained TensorFlow model and returns a probability-based prediction for each image through HTTP requests.
                </p>
                <p>
                    The system is intended as an educational and research implementation for the thesis. Its predictions should be interpreted as model outputs, not as a replacement for professional medical diagnosis.
                </p>

